{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYGHWBLMq7gxfWAzcTSq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything yet, because the README already has the policy. Its \"Loan periods\" section says every kind of item gets 21 days from this autumn. The mismatch is in the code. `LOAN_DAYS` in `loans.py` still has the old periods: novel 14, magazine 7, dvd 7, tool 5, reference 3. The two tests in `test_loans.py` check the old novel and dvd values.\n\nA test of the new policy would fail against the current code. Making it pass means changing what the desk screen prints for due dates, and I didn't want to do that without asking.\n\nWhich do you want?\n\n1. **Fix the code to match the README (my default).** I'd set every `LOAN_DAYS` entry to 21 and update the two existing tests to expect 21 days. I'd also add a test that every kind in `LOAN_DAYS` gets 21 days, so a new kind can't be added at a different length by accident. The README stays as it is.\n2. **The README is wrong, and the policy isn't a flat 21 days.** Send me the real periods per kind. I'd update the README, the code and the tests to match.\n3. **Change only the README and add a test.** Tell me what the README should say. The test would then fail against the code until the code is fixed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":39220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":377},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23a9c238-812b-4b29-8b84-230f267edd40","uuid":"a540f885-ee15-403c-bc5e-974cac153934","timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:28:50.707Z","request_id":"req_011CgYGHVpzsv6jCBzcW6eVM"}
